{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals","id":1162533,"title":"Do the Mists no longer affect other supernaturals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-25T12:34:39-08:00","id":1162533,"title":"Do the Mists no longer affect other supernaturals?","content":"Hello. I've reading C20 and noticed the entry that explains the Mists only mentions its effect specifically on mortals and changelings. Am I missing anything or are supernaturals actually immune to it now? I remember it explicitly said it affected other supernaturals as much as normal humans in 2nd ed. but I can't find anything like that in C20.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T17:59:29-08:00","id":1162586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals#post1162533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I've reading C20 and noticed the entry that explains the Mists only mentions its effect specifically on mortals and changelings. Am I missing anything or are supernaturals actually immune to it now? I remember it explicitly said it affected other supernaturals as much as normal humans in 2nd ed. but I can't find anything like that in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernaturals seem to also have much lower Banalities across the board, but their interactions with Changelings do seem to indicate long term understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T07:33:25-08:00","id":1162718,"title":"","content":"To be honest I had hoped someone would tell me I missed it and it does affect supernaturals as well lol. The fact that supernatural aren't mentioned at all is what puzzles me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T08:02:28-08:00","id":1162722,"title":"","content":"I just interpret &quot;mortal&quot; as meaning &quot;not of the Dreaming&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T08:21:37-08:00","id":1162723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1162722#post1162722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just interpret &quot;mortal&quot; as meaning &quot;not of the Dreaming&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As will I when I run my own games, but right now I'm in a mixed game (with the ST being unfamiliar to 2nd edition). I did stuff imagining it worked just like in 2nd ed and am paying the price for it lol.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I couldn't find anything regarding enchantment working on prodigals either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T08:50:34-08:00","id":1162730,"title":"","content":"Those sound like pretty poor rulings to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T05:58:03-08:00","id":1162969,"title":"","content":"Having immunity it's more &quot;heavy&quot;, rules wise, than not having immunity. Or so I think.<br /> <br /> Generally, you assume that a fireball will affect everyone that's not stated to be immune to fire, because that's how fire works. You don't need to specify that &quot;fire works on prodigals&quot;<br /> Thus, not stating that a power works on a specific type of creature doesn't mean that it doesn't. <br /> <br /> Then again, in WoD, &quot;mortal&quot; usually means &quot;normal human&quot;. There's a lot of powers of every splat that work only on &quot;mortals&quot;. If prodigals are treated as &quot;mortal&quot; or not it's something the ST has to rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T12:21:40-08:00","id":1163306,"title":"","content":"Technically, the fae think all the other supernaturals are Prodigals (i.e., long-lost fae). So in that light, it arguably still applies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:40:29-08:00","id":1163379,"title":"","content":"None of the supernatural NPCs perspectives make sense unless they either have profoundly lower banality than your average human or immunity to the mists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:48:22-08:00","id":1163588,"title":"","content":"Many of them do have lower Banality. But you can shift ratings up or down according to taste. I like the idea characters can hide in plain sight, but sometimes, for ease, you need other splats to see the fairies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:12:05-08:00","id":1164142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1163588#post1163588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many of them do have lower Banality. But you can shift ratings up or down according to taste. I like the idea characters can hide in plain sight, but sometimes, for ease, you need other splats to see the fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it describes Get of Fenris hunting changelings, it seems like at the very least they should have changeling level banality setup..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T05:13:54-08:00","id":1164227,"title":"","content":"Why changeling-level? They're not fae. Besides, you can fudge it with rites, gifts and oaths. Granted, it would be better if the rules made it clear how these beings interact. Maybe there's a Merit or a Background that could be created to allow supers to see fae? The trait might also have an umbrella effect for companions, so that a Fenris elder with the Background/Merit can inspire his followers to temporarily see the fae too, so long as he maintains command with a series of Leadership rolls. <br /> <br /> So let's call this Faerie Sight (5-point Merit). It allows the user to see and touch chimerical reality--although it also allows chimerical reality to see and touch him. Glamour can also be absorbed to replenish vitae, Quintessence or Gnosis, but consuming Glamour reduces any Willpower rolls by two dice until the Glamour is spent. Gaining Glamour in this way may draw unwelcome attention. The power must be activated like Auspex one, but it's a reflexive action (this stops werewolves constantly being assailed by chimera, for example).<br /> <br /> On a successful Charisma + Leadership roll (difficulty 8), he can lead his followers/troops/companions in seeing/touching the fae for the purposes of socialising or combat. This would allow war-parties to hunt the fae or for questing supers to engage with them and otherwise form bonds, oaths and enmities. The effect lasts for one scene per success, and then he must roll again. If he fails any of the rolls, his companions lose their Faerie Sight and he cannot attempt again for the remainder of the scene. If he botches, he temporarily loses it too and can't regain his ability for 24 hours. Characters with Faerie Sight don't succumb to the memory-modifying effects of the Mists, but their companions do (consider their Banality rating to be two dots lower when it comes to remembering this specific episode only).<br /> <br /> What do you think? This is all just off the top of my head...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-01-2017, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T22:52:13-08:00","id":1164472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1164227#post1164227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why changeling-level? They're not fae..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are conflating two things. I don't feel supernaturals should be able to see into the dreaming. I think they should be able to engage in things like they are described doing such as an active emnity between the Get of Fenris and Sidhe without the werewolves completely forgetting what happened.<br /> <br /> And no, creating a new Rite/merit/etc doesn't help this at all. It the whole air breathing mermaid thing(both declaring mermaids can't breath air and then coming up with methods for them to do so).<br /> <br /> Really all I'm saying is Prodigals who interact regularly with changelings should have low banality and function as 2 points lower as long as they regularly engage their personal sort of wars.<br /> <br /> Plus low banality isn't really an advantage for non fae. High banality is actually rather a good thing for non fae as it protects you from fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T12:52:12-08:00","id":1164858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1164142#post1164142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> it describes Get of Fenris hunting changelings, it seems like at the very least they should have changeling level banality setup..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mists aren't your &quot;I don't believe in faeries&quot; rating. It's how much you remember about interacting with Glamour based on your Banality. &quot;My pack met up with some Changelings and now three of my pack are dead and I don't remember what happened, so I'm going to kill every Changeling I see&quot; is perfectly compatible with the Mists and having Banality 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:29:48-08:00","id":1164907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1162586#post1162586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supernaturals seem to also have much lower Banalities across the board, but their interactions with Changelings do seem to indicate long term understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That only makes sense, considering they aren't exactly normal people, either.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> Oh, sure, spirits of nature exist. I deal with them on a regular basis. <i>But fairies</i>? Come on, that sounds ridiculous!<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> So you figured out a way to bring your imagination to life, but have a hard time doing it around normal society? <i>Are you sure</i> you're not just one of us?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: </b>We have a word for people who run around fighting imaginary enemies with a cardboard tube and tin foil shield, and it's not 'fairy!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T19:18:08-08:00","id":1164945,"title":"","content":"By the way, the Mists are also what keeps mortals from seeing a Changeling's fae mien. So apparently the OPs ST got rid of that for werewolves and vampires too?<br /> <br /> At least this means supernaturals in the World of Darkness are vulnerable to Chimerical damage in this game, as that's another thing the Mists protects unenchanted mortals from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 12-03-2017, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T04:31:01-08:00","id":1165011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1164945#post1164945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, the Mists are also what keeps mortals from seeing a Changeling's fae mien. So apparently the OPs ST got rid of that for werewolves and vampires too?<br /> <br /> At least this means supernaturals in the World of Darkness are vulnerable to Chimerical damage in this game, as that's another thing the Mists protects unenchanted mortals from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source for that claim?<br /> <br /> As for my ST, he is following C20 strictly as it is written. And in the book there is absolutely nothing that says the mists either affects supernaturals or that 'mortals' include supernatural as well. I showed him 2nd edition to try to convince him but just got a 'well that's not the case here' and that's what led me to make this thread, to clarify that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:24:03-08:00","id":1165844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1165011#post1165011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have a source for that claim?<br /> <br /> As for my ST, he is following C20 strictly as it is written. And in the book there is absolutely nothing that says the mists either affects supernaturals or that 'mortals' include supernatural as well. I showed him 2nd edition to try to convince him but just got a 'well that's not the case here' and that's what led me to make this thread, to clarify that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offence, but your ST seems to have missed the spirit of the text, if not the letter. The Mists are more than just forgetting about faeries, and they effect everyone (even the fae) in one way or another. They're similar to the Delirium and the Fog in one sense, but they also play a similar role to the Gauntlet in that the Mists are also the metaphysical barriers between human and faerie worlds, and between the various layers of the faerie world (the Vale of Mists is the fabric between each layer, where the Mists are at their strongest). <br /> <br /> I'd have to check C20 again to see how clear that is in the core book, but Dreams &amp; Nightmares makes it clear that the Mists act like the Shroud or the Gauntlet in certain places.<br /> <br /> If the Mists do not apply, that causes multiple problems because they work both ways--they protect the fae but they protect non-fae too. If they don't apply to supernaturals, they lose that protection. The world also loses its metaphysical integrity, in that the Dreaming would no longer be separate from the Autumn World for supernaturals.<br /> <br /> If the Mists no longer apply to supernaturals (which is stupid, because they apply even to changelings), then one world slips easily into the next. Set foot outside your haven and step into a Nightmare Realm. Go to sleep and find yourself in the Deep Dreaming. It seems a huge mistake to just ignore the Mists.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your ST is separating the Mists' forgetting properties from its Gauntlet-like properties, but either way, it implies he's not really grasped the concept fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:46:39-08:00","id":1165849,"title":"","content":"This Mists are the Dreaming's defense against Banality. They affect anything with a Banality rating. In the context of Changeling: The Dreaming, that's everything living (or un-living) on Earth. Just because C20 doesn't provide blanket statements about how much Banality a given clan, tribe, or tradition has doesn't mean that other supernaturals lack Banality for the purposes of crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:06:19-08:00","id":1165858,"title":"","content":"Double checked: refer your ST to pp.45-6 of C20. It's clear that the Mists are a 'barrier' between worlds, and that the Forgetting is just one effect of that barrier (but one that even changelings succumb to).<br /> <br /> That section also suggests that its mortals' Banality ratings that make them susceptible to the Forgetting, not their mortality per se: 'The force of Banality in most mortals keeps them from perceiving anything outside of what they believe can exist.' It's Banality, not mortality, that causes the Forgetting. Specifically, it's the interaction between Banality and the Mists that causes it (p.45), so any being with high enough Banality will be affected.<br /> <br /> The section on Prodigals from p.345 onwards, explicitly refers to them as fae. Thus, at the very least, the same system should apply to supernaturals as to faeries when it comes to Banality. Also of note, these creatures aren't devoid of Banality--they all have ratings given, and so experience the consequences and benefits thereof.<br /> <br /> Also of note: p.347 explicitly says it's Toreadors' powers of sight (Auspex) that allows them to see fae. The implication being that vampires without this power can't see the fae naturally. Extrapolate as necessary (Mind/Spirit, Heightened Senses, certain Gifts are probably required to see faeries).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:04:46-08:00","id":1165872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section on Prodigals from p.345 onwards, explicitly refers to them as fae. Thus, at the very least, the same system should apply to supernaturals as to faeries when it comes to Banality. Also of note, these creatures aren't devoid of Banality--they all have ratings given, and so experience the consequences and benefits thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you used to need Fae realm to affect them, if I remember correctly, so it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'The force of Banality in most mortals keeps them from perceiving anything outside of what they believe can exist.' </div> </div> </div>So mortals can't remember because Banality prevents them from seeing things outside what they believe. However supernatural belief tends to be a bit more complicated than that: For instance, Splats doesn't count as witnesses in Mage regardless of their beliefs. Only the very rare &quot;sleepwalker&quot; count as witnesses-for other mages or beings, it would seem that they believe in the impossible at some subconscious level because the belief system of the supernatural or her personal experience doesn't seem to matter, they just don't count-unlike mortals, that may or may not count as witness depending on their experience and beliefs (to the point that one mortal that may not count for one Paradigm but count for another).<br /> <br /> Pondering in all of that, I think that it would make sense that supers count as faes for the purposes of remembering, but not necessarily for other stuff because this would be a function of them being &quot;awakened creatures&quot;unless they have a Defect that makes them count as mortals (like Sleepwalker in Mage). This would explain the interactions and the need for aditional powers to see faes and fae stuff (something that Faes can do naturally. Perhaps because they have an innate Talent to do so that other splats don't have?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-07-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:42:31-08:00","id":1165881,"title":"","content":"Traditionally, other supernaturals count as mortals for the purposes of Realms and the Mists. There haven't been any crossover rules written for C20, but previous crossover rules will work fine (or as fine as the crossover rules ever worked) with C20.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head though, I'd probably switch things up so that supernaturals require Fae 3 to affect since from the Changeling perspective, they're all wayward creatures of the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T03:20:59-08:00","id":1166042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1165849#post1165849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Mists are the Dreaming's defense against Banality. They affect anything with a Banality rating. In the context of Changeling: The Dreaming, that's everything living (or un-living) on Earth. Just because C20 doesn't provide blanket statements about how much Banality a given clan, tribe, or tradition has doesn't mean that other supernaturals lack Banality for the purposes of crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. To be honest I was shocked when my ST said there wasn't anything saying that it affected other supernaturals because I never dwelled into it for assuming it was the same as 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> The issue here isn't that it doesn't specifically mention a tribe or clan but that it only addresses 'mortals' being affected by the Mists. Personally I've always thought that mortals should include other non-changeling supernaturals but I don't really blame my ST for interpreting otherwise. C20 has changed quite a bit of 2nd ed. fundamentals so for all I know this could be another change too. 2nd also uses the term mortals but makes it clear that it includes unenchanted supernaturals (page 208), while C20 does not. I made this thread to try and clarify that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, you used to need Fae realm to affect them, if I remember correctly, so it makes sense. </div> </div> </div>From CtD 2nd ed. page 188:<br /> 'Actor: This Realm concerns itself with mortals. The higher the Realm, the less the caster must personally know the person. This Realm includes supernatural beings such as vampires, wraiths, etc., but not other fae.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T09:17:08-08:00","id":1166292,"title":"","content":"The Mists aren't about paradigms, that's Mage territory. The Mists are part of why most mortals don't believe in Changelings, but you *can* have a Banality 10 hunter of the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T11:59:54-08:00","id":1166316,"title":"","content":"Your ST is wrong. Refer to the Banality ratings in the back of C20. Anything with Banality is affected by the Mists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T05:06:35-08:00","id":1167577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1166042#post1166042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From CtD 2nd ed. page 188:<br /> 'Actor: This Realm concerns itself with mortals. The higher the Realm, the less the caster must personally know the person. This Realm includes supernatural beings such as vampires, wraiths, etc., but not other fae.'</div> </div> </div> </div>The actor bit in C20 is almost identical. They use the term prodigial iirc. Also interacting with other changelings lower effective banality by two for changelings. It's in the myst section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","user":"Monkeydjie","date":".  Clarification 12-14-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:29:34-08:00","id":1168556,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of ok with supernaturals being immune to the mists, so long as that immunity carries over to the Delerium, bring a witness to vulgar magick and any other &quot;cover our ass&quot; inherent powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:49:04-08:00","id":1168608,"title":"","content":"Changelings have always been immune to the Delerium, Fog, count not witnesses for Magic, etc. That's probably why the ST thought the Mists work the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T15:42:42-08:00","id":1168656,"title":"","content":"The important thing to remember about the Mists is that it, unlike Delirium, Fog or being a witness for Magick, affects Changelings themselves as well so the question is should the other supernatural really be more immune to the Mists than Changelings themselves. I personally think not. Also like pointed out Prodigals are affects through Actor Realm aka the \u201dmortal\u201d Realm. That is to say in general they are affected in the same manner as Mortals by Changeling magic. <br /> <br /> I do believe it an oversight to leave out an exact sentence mentioning that the Prodigals are affected by the Mists just like everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T17:12:02-08:00","id":1168678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkeydjie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1167577#post1167577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The actor bit in C20 is almost identical. They use the term prodigial iirc. Also interacting with other changelings lower effective banality by two for changelings. It's in the myst section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that. I quoted the person who said you needed Fae to affect prodigals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The important thing to remember about the Mists is that it, unlike Delirium, Fog or being a witness for Magick, affects Changelings themselves as well so the question is should the other supernatural really be more immune to the Mists than Changelings themselves. I personally think not. Also like pointed out Prodigals are affects through Actor Realm aka the \u201dmortal\u201d Realm. That is to say in general they are affected in the same manner as Mortals by Changeling magic.<br /> <br /> I do believe it an oversight to leave out an exact sentence mentioning that the Prodigals are affected by the Mists just like everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with every single word you posted, thank you.<br /> <br /> In other news, after I showed this thread to the ST and pointed out that one of the writers said it works, he finally backed down and accepted it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T18:25:58-08:00","id":1168692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1162533-do-the-mists-no-longer-affect-other-supernaturals?p=1162586#post1162586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supernaturals seem to also have much lower Banalities across the board, but their interactions with Changelings do seem to indicate long term understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with this. If you look toward the end of the 20th edition book, you'll notice banality varies for the templates except for most technocracy mages which have an incredibly high banality, almost as much if not as much as a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23616-phantasmology","name":"Phantasmology","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}